{"content_hash": "30ef0617fcc65389", "version_id": 855, "article_id": 86, "level_code": "en_c1", "lang": "en", "level": 5, "level_label": "C1 高级", "title": "Apple brings noise cancelling to its cheaper AirPods 5", "title_zh": "苹果把主动降噪下放到更便宜的 AirPods 5", "has_translation": true, "topic": "lifestyle", "source": "sspai", "source_url": "https://sspai.com/post/118122", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1662946834880-99adabd21f80?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8NHx8dGRzJTIwcmV2aWV3JTIwYXBwbGV8ZW58MHwwfHx8MTc5MzY3NDkzM3ww&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by BoliviaInteligente on Unsplash", "author": "BoliviaInteligente", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@boliviainteligente?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/apple-logo-in-glass-cube-fN4YeoA14OI?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(104, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(142, 46%, 48%)", "label": "LIFESTYLE", "seed": "a388a2c1c56a"}}, "published_date": "2026-11-03", "word_count": 253, "reading_minutes": 1.3, "lead": "Apple's AirPods 5 pushes active noise cancelling into the sub-1,000-yuan bracket, a feature once reserved for pricier models. But a near-identical shell and modest battery gains leave the upgrade looking uneven, and reviewers are split on the tuning.", "lead_zh": "苹果 AirPods 5 把主动降噪带进了千元以内的价位，这项功能过去只属于更贵的型号。但几乎一模一样的外壳和有限的续航提升，让这次升级显得有些不够全面，评测者对调音也褒贬不一。", "preview": "Two years after its last half-in-ear review, TDS Studio bought the standard AirPods 5, which shares the H2 chip with its predecessor. Visual", "preview_zh": "时隔两年，TDS Studio 再次评测半入耳式耳机，这次自费购买了标准版 AirPods 5，它和上一代一样搭载 H2 芯片。外观上它几乎和 AirPods 4 无法分辨：同样的白色亮面塑料、同样小巧的充电盒，两代耳机甚至能互换充电。真正的变化藏在内部，苹果重新设计了声学腔体以", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 838, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/86/en_c1.mp3", "duration": 105.475, "size_bytes": 633744, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 293, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@0cb59f2/content/data/versions/855.json", "paragraphs": ["Two years after its last half-in-ear review, TDS Studio bought the standard AirPods 5, which shares the H2 chip with its predecessor. Visually it is all but indistinguishable from the AirPods 4: same white glossy plastic, same tiny case, and the earbuds can even be swapped between the two generations for charging. The real changes sit inside, where Apple reworked the acoustic chamber to improve airflow.", "Apple splits the range in two. The 999-yuan wired version loses the case speaker, wireless charging and Precision Finding, leaving only the buds themselves to emit a locating chime. Pay 1,149 yuan and you regain those features plus swipe gestures on the stem. Both versions now carry IP57 dust and water resistance, up from IP54, surviving up to 30 minutes submerged at one metre.", "Noise cancelling is the headline. Against the AirPods 4 ANC and Huawei's Freebuds 7, the AirPods 5 suppresses steady low-frequency rumble and lower-midrange voices far more effectively, edging close to AirPods Pro 2 territory. Its adaptive compensation after a fit shift is the quickest in the half-in-ear class, reacting almost instantly, and transparency remains natural and conversational.", "Wind noise during calls is the weak spot: with wind from the side or behind, the AirPods 5 still let through noticeable interference, trailing the AirPods 4 and Freebuds 7. Sound leans bass-heavy by default, thicker than the AirPods 4's brighter balance, flattering hip-hop and trap but blurring overall composure. TDS ranks it top of the half-in-ear noise-cancelling field, though some in-ear rivals still come first."], "paragraphs_zh": ["时隔两年，TDS Studio 再次评测半入耳式耳机，这次自费购买了标准版 AirPods 5，它和上一代一样搭载 H2 芯片。外观上它几乎和 AirPods 4 无法分辨：同样的白色亮面塑料、同样小巧的充电盒，两代耳机甚至能互换充电。真正的变化藏在内部，苹果重新设计了声学腔体以改善气流。", "苹果把这一代分成两个版本。999 元的有线充电版砍掉了盒身扬声器、无线充电和精确查找，只能靠耳机本身发出寻找提示音。多花 1,149 元才能找回这些功能，外加柄部滑动操作。两个版本都从 IP54 升级到 IP57 防尘防水，可在 1 米深水下停留最长 30 分钟。", "降噪是最大卖点。对比 AirPods 4 ANC 和华为 Freebuds 7，AirPods 5 对稳定低频轰鸣和中低人声的压制明显更强，已接近 AirPods Pro 2 的水平。佩戴松动后的自适应补偿是半入耳阵营中最快的，几乎瞬间完成，通透模式的自然度和对话可用性也依旧出色。", "通话抗风噪是短板：侧面或背后来风时，AirPods 5 仍有明显干扰，落后于 AirPods 4 和 Freebuds 7。默认调音偏重低频，比 AirPods 4 更厚，适合嘻哈和 trap，但整体平衡感受损。TDS 仍把它排在半入耳降噪耳机首位，不过一些入耳型号依然更靠前。"], "body": "Two years after its last half-in-ear review, TDS Studio bought the standard AirPods 5, which shares the H2 chip with its predecessor. Visually it is all but indistinguishable from the AirPods 4: same white glossy plastic, same tiny case, and the earbuds can even be swapped between the two generations for charging. The real changes sit inside, where Apple reworked the acoustic chamber to improve airflow.\n\nApple splits the range in two. The 999-yuan wired version loses the case speaker, wireless charging and Precision Finding, leaving only the buds themselves to emit a locating chime. Pay 1,149 yuan and you regain those features plus swipe gestures on the stem. Both versions now carry IP57 dust and water resistance, up from IP54, surviving up to 30 minutes submerged at one metre.\n\nNoise cancelling is the headline. Against the AirPods 4 ANC and Huawei's Freebuds 7, the AirPods 5 suppresses steady low-frequency rumble and lower-midrange voices far more effectively, edging close to AirPods Pro 2 territory. Its adaptive compensation after a fit shift is the quickest in the half-in-ear class, reacting almost instantly, and transparency remains natural and conversational.\n\nWind noise during calls is the weak spot: with wind from the side or behind, the AirPods 5 still let through noticeable interference, trailing the AirPods 4 and Freebuds 7. Sound leans bass-heavy by default, thicker than the AirPods 4's brighter balance, flattering hip-hop and trap but blurring overall composure. TDS ranks it top of the half-in-ear noise-cancelling field, though some in-ear rivals still come first.", "body_zh": "时隔两年，TDS Studio 再次评测半入耳式耳机，这次自费购买了标准版 AirPods 5，它和上一代一样搭载 H2 芯片。外观上它几乎和 AirPods 4 无法分辨：同样的白色亮面塑料、同样小巧的充电盒，两代耳机甚至能互换充电。真正的变化藏在内部，苹果重新设计了声学腔体以改善气流。\n\n苹果把这一代分成两个版本。999 元的有线充电版砍掉了盒身扬声器、无线充电和精确查找，只能靠耳机本身发出寻找提示音。多花 1,149 元才能找回这些功能，外加柄部滑动操作。两个版本都从 IP54 升级到 IP57 防尘防水，可在 1 米深水下停留最长 30 分钟。\n\n降噪是最大卖点。对比 AirPods 4 ANC 和华为 Freebuds 7，AirPods 5 对稳定低频轰鸣和中低人声的压制明显更强，已接近 AirPods Pro 2 的水平。佩戴松动后的自适应补偿是半入耳阵营中最快的，几乎瞬间完成，通透模式的自然度和对话可用性也依旧出色。\n\n通话抗风噪是短板：侧面或背后来风时，AirPods 5 仍有明显干扰，落后于 AirPods 4 和 Freebuds 7。默认调音偏重低频，比 AirPods 4 更厚，适合嘻哈和 trap，但整体平衡感受损。TDS 仍把它排在半入耳降噪耳机首位，不过一些入耳型号依然更靠前。", "text": "Two years after its last half-in-ear review, TDS Studio bought the standard AirPods 5, which shares the H2 chip with its predecessor. Visually it is all but indistinguishable from the AirPods 4: same white glossy plastic, same tiny case, and the earbuds can even be swapped between the two generations for charging. The real changes sit inside, where Apple reworked the acoustic chamber to improve airflow. Apple splits the range in two. The 999-yuan wired version loses the case speaker, wireless charging and Precision Finding, leaving only the buds themselves to emit a locating chime. Pay 1,149 yuan and you regain those features plus swipe gestures on the stem. Both versions now carry IP57 dust and water resistance, up from IP54, surviving up to 30 minutes submerged at one metre. Noise cancelling is the headline. Against the AirPods 4 ANC and Huawei's Freebuds 7, the AirPods 5 suppresses steady low-frequency rumble and lower-midrange voices far more effectively, edging close to AirPods Pro 2 territory. Its adaptive compensation after a fit shift is the quickest in the half-in-ear class, reacting almost instantly, and transparency remains natural and conversational. Wind noise during calls is the weak spot: with wind from the side or behind, the AirPods 5 still let through noticeable interference, trailing the AirPods 4 and Freebuds 7. Sound leans bass-heavy by default, thicker than the AirPods 4's brighter balance, flattering hip-hop and trap but blurring overall composure. TDS ranks it top of the half-in-ear noise-cancelling field, though some in-ear rivals still come first.", "vocab": [{"word": "indistinguishable", "pos": "adj", "zh": "无法分辨的", "note": "常与 from 连用，indistinguishable from sth", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "predecessor", "pos": "noun", "zh": "前代产品；前任", "note": "科技评测中常指上一代型号", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "rework", "pos": "verb", "zh": "重新设计；改造", "note": "比 change 更强调结构性改动", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "submerge", "pos": "verb", "zh": "浸没；没入水中", "note": "防水等级描述常用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "suppress", "pos": "verb", "zh": "抑制；压制", "note": "降噪语境高频词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "rumble", "pos": "noun", "zh": "低沉的轰鸣声", "note": "指地铁、飞机等低频噪音", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "edge close to", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "接近；逼近", "note": "表示差距很小", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "compensation", "pos": "noun", "zh": "补偿；校正", "note": "此处指佩戴变化后的自适应调整", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "transparency", "pos": "noun", "zh": "通透模式", "note": "耳机术语，与降噪相对", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "trail", "pos": "verb", "zh": "落后于", "note": "trail sb/sth 表示不如对方", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "lean", "pos": "verb", "zh": "偏向；倾向", "note": "lean + 形容词，描述调音风格", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "flatter", "pos": "verb", "zh": "使…显得更好；讨好", "note": "此处指低频让某些曲风更出彩", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "blur", "pos": "verb", "zh": "使模糊；削弱清晰度", "note": "可指声音结像变糊", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "composure", "pos": "noun", "zh": "整体的沉稳感；平衡感", "note": "此处引申指声音的整体把控", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T03:02:11.555592", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Two", "s": 0.275, "e": 0.45, "sm": 275, "em": 450, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "years", "s": 0.45, "e": 0.75, "sm": 450, "em": 750, "cs": 4, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, 